{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>You and Pinchas.</b> This teaches that Pinchas was weighted equally against all of them (Sifrei). And why did Pinchas go and not Elazar? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: He who began the mitzvah — who killed Cozbi daughter of Zur — shall finish it. Another interpretation — he went to avenge the vengeance of Yosef, his mother's father, as it says ״וְהַמְּדָנִים מָכְרוּ אֹתוֹ״ (Genesis 37). And from where do we know that Pinchas's mother was of the seed of Yosef? As it says ״מִבְּנוֹת פּוּטִיאֵל״ (Exodus 6) — of the seed of Yitro, who fattened calves for idolatry, and of the seed of Yosef, who fattened [pitted] his inclination (Sotah 43). Another interpretation — he was anointed for war (ibid.)." "<b>And the sacred vessels.</b> This is the Ark and the Tzitz. For Bilam was with them and would make the kings of Midian fly by sorcery, and he himself would fly with them. He showed them the Tzitz, on which the Name is engraved, and they fell — therefore it says ״עַל חַלְלֵיהֶם״ regarding the kings of Midian, because they fall onto the corpses from the air. And likewise regarding Bilam it is written ״עַל חַלְלֵיהֶם״ in the book of Joshua (Tanchuma)." "<b>In his hand.</b> In his domain — and likewise (Numbers 21) ״וַיִּקַּח אֶת כָּל אַרְצוֹ מִיָּדוֹ״ (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "על חלליהם in comment 1 (cited from Joshua 13:22) is spelled identically to the phrase in our verse (Numbers 31:8); the point is the verbal echo between the two verses."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:26.702263080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}